<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04196/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04196/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04196/>;
    dc:modified '2006-10-02T18:26:59'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'graphite furnace atomic absorption spectroscopy'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The sample is volatilised on a graphite platform contained within a graphite tube and its temperature is systematically raised according to a predetermined programme. The resultant vapour is illuminated by a light source with an emission spectrum matched to the analyte of interest. Radiation absorbed by chemically unbound atoms is determined by analysing the transmitted energy relative to the incident energy at each frequency, which is proportional to the elemental concentrations.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S04::S04196'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04196/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04196/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04196/>;
    dc:modified '2006-10-02T18:26:59'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'spectrométrie d\'absorption atomique avec four en graphite (GFAAS)'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The sample is volatilised on a graphite platform contained within a graphite tube and its temperature is systematically raised according to a predetermined programme. The resultant vapour is illuminated by a light source with an emission spectrum matched to the analyte of interest. Radiation absorbed by chemically unbound atoms is determined by analysing the transmitted energy relative to the incident energy at each frequency, which is proportional to the elemental concentrations.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S04::S04196'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04196/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04196/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04196/>;
    dc:modified '2006-10-02T18:26:59'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'graphite furnace atomic absorption spectroscopy'@en ;
    skos:definition 'L\'échantillon est vaporisé sur une plate-forme graphite placée à l\'intérieur d\'un tube en graphite dont la température augmente progressivement selon un programme pré-défini. La vapeur résultante est ensuite irradié par une lumière dont le spectre d\'émission correspond à l\'analyte d\'intérêt. La radiation absorbée par les atomes à l\'état fondamental est déterminée par comparaison de l\'énergie transmise par rapport à l\'énergie incidente pour chaque fréquence. La quantité de radiation absorbée est proportionnelle à la concentration de l\'élément.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S04::S04196'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04196/1/> .
