    dc:modified '2006-10-02T18:26:59'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mechanical bathythermograph'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A device used prior to the 1980s for obtaining a record of temperature against depth (strictly speaking, pressure) in the upper 300m of the ocean. The thermal element was a xylene-filled copper coil, which actuated a stylus through a Bourdon tube. The pressure element was a copper aneroid capsule that moved a smoked glass slide at right angles to the motion of the stylus. Data were usually distributed as enlarged photographs of the trace etched on the glass slide.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S04::S04261'^^xsd:string .
