    skos:definition 'A temperature sensor co-located with the conductivity cell in the thermosalinograph used solely to supply data for the conversion of temperature to salinity. The conductivity cell is often located in laboratory space and therefore this sensor returns values significantly different from ambient sea temperature.'@en ;
